@startuml pipeline-status
title What is actually wired, as of this review

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

rectangle "lib.rs::extractor\n(#[proc_macro_derive(Extractor)])" as Entry #E8F4EA

rectangle "StructExtraction\n<&'ast DeriveInput>" as S #E8F4EA
rectangle "FieldExtraction\n<&'ast Field>" as F #E8F4EA
rectangle "TransformationExtraction\n<&'ast Attribute>" as T #FFD9D9
rectangle "SyntaxFieldAttributeExtraction\n<&'ast Attribute>" as Y #FFF4E5

rectangle "Processor" as P #EEEEEE
rectangle "Generator" as G #EEEEEE

Entry --> S : parse_macro_input\nthen extract_from
S --> F : extract_each(data.fields.iter())
F --> T : extract_each(field.attrs.iter())

S ..> P : Extracted<..>
P ..> G

note bottom of T
  **todo!()** — panics if reached.
  Nothing currently reaches it.
  Blocked on #syntax/traits.
end note

note bottom of Y
  Works, and is tested — but is driven
  ONLY by base/syntax/worked.rs, never
  by the macro path. #syntax/not-driven
end note

note bottom of P
  comment-only stub in both crates.
  Extractor::Output is deliberately
  unbounded until this exists.
end note

legend right
  |<#E8F4EA>| live on the macro path |
  |<#FFF4E5>| works, tested, not wired |
  |<#FFD9D9>| todo!() — would panic |
  |<#EEEEEE>| does not exist yet |
endlegend

note as Gap
  **The load-bearing gap**

  The extraction tree is BUILT and then
  nobody reads it. ""fields"" and
  ""transformation"" carry
  ""#[allow(dead_code)]"" saying exactly
  that. lib.rs renders top-level reasons
  and emits a stub — the recursive walk
  is #syntax/render.
end note

Gap .. P

@enduml
